          "structuredContent": {
            "modules": [
              {
                "alignment": "left",
                "alt": null,
                "caption": null,
                "embedUrl": null,
                "height": null,
                "imageId": null,
                "originalUrl": null,
                "text": "<p><strong><strong>This event is for UAL students and staff only, a valid UAL ID card will be needed to enter the site and attend.</strong></strong></p><p>Diasporic Films is a series of free contextualised screenings celebrating and depicting diaspora communities or made by diaspora filmmakers. The themes are often reflective of identity, representation, displacement and visibility. The series seeks to highlight how culture, heritage and experience can open dialogues about our own positionalities, making us consider how such themes can intersect with our own practices.</p><p>The series runs from Wednesday 7 October 2026 to Wednesday 25 November 2026, 6pm-8.30pm, in London College of Communication, Lecture Theatre C (LTC).</p><p><strong><strong>Full screening list:</strong></strong></p><ul><li>07/10, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=seHuOmdcJqg\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=seHuOmdcJqg\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">MISSISSIPPI MASALA</a> (1991) - The vibrant cultures of India, Uganda, and the American South come together in this look at the complexities of love, via racism, colourism, culture clash, and displacement.</li><li>14/10, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wWFRdG4y0eg\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wWFRdG4y0eg\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">RUDEBOY: THE STORY OF TROJAN RECORDS</a> (2018) - The story of an iconic reggae and ska record label and part of the revolution that unfolded between Jamaican and British youth culture in the late ‘60s and early ‘70s Britain.</li><li>21/10, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ylaxvOZs1Xw\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ylaxvOZs1Xw\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">DRYLONGSO</a> (1998) - A woman in a photography class, Pica, begins taking pictures of black men out of fear they will soon be extinct. <strong><strong>To be screened in Lecture Theatre A</strong></strong></li><li>28/10, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kA244xewjcI\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kA244xewjcI\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">PAST LIVES</a> (2023) - Two childhood friends are separated after one's family emigrates from South Korea. Two decades later, they are reunited in New York for one fateful week.</li><li>04/11, *SURPRISE STUDENT SCREENING PICK + INTRO.* - Announced week of event.</li><li>11/11, *SURPRISE STUDENT SCREENING PICK + INTRO.* - Announced week of event.</li><li>18/11, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WQsoGg-O9yE\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WQsoGg-O9yE\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">NEWS FROM HOME</a> (1976) - Director Chantal Akerman reads letters sent to her from her mother in Belgium, against a tableau of shots of 1970s New York.</li><li>25/11, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NWLvgMbWQF0\" title=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NWLvgMbWQF0\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">QUEEN OF MY DREAMS</a> (2023) - A Bollywood-infused story of the love and war between a queer Canadian woman and her Pakistani mother, spanning across decades and continents.</li></ul><p>Doors will be open from 6PM, screenings start promptly at 6.15PM. Late comers are welcome but please appreciate and respect the attending audience when entering the room.</p><p>Diasporic Films is organised and run by Hamish Mèk Chohan (Head of Academic Support), any questions pertaining to the screenings or attendance can be directed to Hamish via email: h.chohan@lcc.arts.ac.uk</p><p>Booking is not required, though appreciated. Seating allowance is subject to room capacity.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Accessibility:</strong></strong><strong><strong> </strong></strong>London College of Communication strives to provide an inclusive and accessible environment for our students and visitors. For full access and route guides for our building, please view our <a href=\"https://www.accessable.co.uk/university-of-the-arts-london-ual/london-college-of-communication-elephant-and-castle\" title=\"https://www.accessable.co.uk/university-of-the-arts-london-ual/london-college-of-communication-elephant-and-castle\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">AccessAble accessibility guide.</a></p><p>If you have any specific access requirements for an event or exhibition at all please contact us by email (<a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/shows-2025-screen-exhibition-tickets-1292586855079?aff=oddtdtcreator\" title=\"https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/shows-2025-screen-exhibition-tickets-1292586855079?aff=oddtdtcreator\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">events@lcc.arts.ac.uk</a>) or phone (020 7514 8498) in advance of your visit, so that we can make any necessary preparations or adjustments.</p><p><strong><strong>Find us:</strong></strong><strong><strong> </strong></strong>London College of Communication is located close to central London in Elephant and Castle. The College is based on a single site within easy reach of various parts of the city, and is well-served by Underground, bus and rail networks. Find out more about getting here on <a href=\"https://www.arts.ac.uk/colleges/london-college-of-communication/about-lcc/find-us\" title=\"https://www.arts.ac.uk/colleges/london-college-of-communication/about-lcc/find-us\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Find Us page</a>.</p><p><strong><strong>Filming and Photography:</strong></strong> Please note that filming and photography may be taking place at this event. Both bigger crowds, smaller groups and individuals may be captured on camera. All imagery and footage may at some point be published on the College website, social media channels, and in print.</p>",
                "type": "text",
                "url": null,
                "width": null
              }
